    "background_story": "Lyla was a talented young editor with a passion for literature. She landed a job at a prestigious publishing house, where she was tasked with revising a classic novel for a modern audience. As she delved into the text, Lyla realized that the original author's tone was too risqu\u00e9 for contemporary readers. She carefully set out to sanitize the content, removing suggestive language and mature themes. However, in doing so, she found herself walking a fine line between preserving the author's intent and appeasing the publisher's demands. Lyla's meticulous editing resulted in a bowdlerized version of the novel, one that was more palatable to modern sensibilities but still retained the essence of the original story. Her work sparked a debate among literary critics about the merits of censorship and the importance of preserving artistic integrity.",
